  "summary": "TSMC's wafer fab campus in north Phoenix, run by its subsidiary TSMC Arizona. Announced in 2020 as a single 5nm fab worth about US$12 billion, it grew to a planned cluster of several leading-edge fabs. The first fab reached high-volume N4 production in the fourth quarter of 2024. The second fab, for 3nm, was structurally complete in 2025 and was being equipped in late 2026 with volume output due in the third quarter of 2027. The third fab (N2 and A16) broke ground in April 2025 and initial work on a fourth began in early 2026. TSMC announced further fabs in March 2025 and July 2026, raising its planned Arizona spending to US$265 billion across fabs, packaging plants and an R&D centre. The site received a final CHIPS Act award of up to US$6.6 billion in direct funding in November 2024.",
